CORE
weak.c
--enforce-contract f _ --pointer-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[f\.precondition_instance\.1\] .*static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: FAILURE$
^\[f\.assertion\.1\] .*implementation is reachable: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.
^\s*ASSUME .*r_ok\(f::
--
A function's own contract that is weaker than its [static N] minimum cannot be
enforced. The generated static-array requires clause is not assumed, so the
contract's one-element is_fresh does not contradict it and the implementation
stays reachable. The minimum is checked at the call to the original
implementation after the explicit requires clauses have been assumed, the same
way as for a separately named contract.
